  <h1>Omekum App AI Readable Document</h1>

  <h2>Purpose</h2>
  <p>
    This document explains the Omekum web app in a structure that is easy for humans,
    Word processors, and AI tools to read. The project is a React and Vite website for
    a digital agency called Omekum.
  </p>

  <h2>Project Summary</h2>
  <table>
    <tr>
      <th>Item</th>
      <th>Value</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Project name</td>
      <td>omekum</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Framework</td>
      <td>React 18 with Vite</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Main app file</td>
      <td>src/App.jsx</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Entry file</td>
      <td>src/main.jsx</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Build output</td>
      <td>dist/</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Local dev URL</td>
      <td>http://127.0.0.1:5173/</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Contact page URL</td>
      <td>http://127.0.0.1:5173/contact</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h2>How To Run</h2>
  <p>Install dependencies if needed:</p>
  <pre>npm install</pre>

  <p>Start the development server:</p>
  <pre>npm run dev -- --host 127.0.0.1</pre>

  <p>Open this URL in a browser:</p>
  <pre>http://127.0.0.1:5173/</pre>

  <p>Build for production:</p>
  <pre>npm run build</pre>

  <p>Preview the production build:</p>
  <pre>npm run preview</pre>

  <h2>App Content</h2>
  <p>
    The app presents Omekum as a practical digital agency that builds websites,
    apps, AI tools, automation systems, dashboards, and custom software.
  </p>

  <h3>Main Sections</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Header navigation: Work, Services, AI Solutions, About, Contact.</li>
    <li>Hero section: Digital products for real-world problems.</li>
    <li>Project numbers section: completed projects, running projects, and AI/automation flows.</li>
    <li>Services section: Digital Products, AI Solutions, Custom Software, Tech Problem Solving.</li>
    <li>About section: Clear communication, practical pricing, fast prototypes, custom solutions, long-term support.</li>
    <li>AI section: Customer support assistants, document automation, lead qualification, dashboards, knowledge chatbots, workflow automation.</li>
    <li>Process section: Understand, design, build, test, launch and improve.</li>
    <li>Work examples: Local Service Booking, AI Support Desk, Operations Dashboard.</li>
    <li>Testimonials section: sample client quotes that should be replaced with real testimonials when available.</li>
    <li>Contact section: Email links to hello@omekum.com.</li>
    <li>Dedicated contact page: Hero section, project inquiry form, direct email option, contact reasons, and next-step trust cues.</li>
    <li>Footer: Services, company links, and email.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Landing Page Project Numbers</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>28+ completed projects.</li>
    <li>06 running projects.</li>
    <li>14 AI and automation flows.</li>
    <li>These are placeholder marketing numbers and should be updated with real Omekum numbers when confirmed.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Landing Page Testimonials</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Testimonial 1: Rohan Mehta, Founder, Local Services Platform.</li>
    <li>Testimonial 2: Anika Sharma, Operations Lead, Support Team.</li>
    <li>Testimonial 3: Vikram Rao, Director, Growing Retail Business.</li>
    <li>These are sample testimonials and should be replaced with real client quotes before public launch if required.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Contact Page Details</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Route: /contact</li>
    <li>Main goal: Encourage users to start a project conversation with Omekum.</li>
    <li>Form fields: name, email, project type, and project details.</li>
    <li>Direct email: hello@omekum.com</li>
    <li>Trust cues: reply within 1 business day, clear next steps, no pressure call, practical budget guidance.</li>
    <li>Contact reasons: build something new, add AI or automation, fix a tech problem.</li>
    <li>Form behavior: opens the user's email app using mailto because no backend is currently connected.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Animation And Motion Scope</h2>
  <p>
    The app includes lightweight CSS animation in areas where motion supports the
    agency story without requiring JavaScript animation libraries.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Hero image uses slow background drift for visual depth.</li>
    <li>Hero content fades and rises on page load.</li>
    <li>Header slides in and the Omekum brand mark has a soft pulse.</li>
    <li>Hero signal strip contains moving labels: Prototype, Automate, Launch, Improve.</li>
    <li>Service cards enter with staggered timing and include a moving scan accent.</li>
    <li>Service accent bars animate through the brand colors.</li>
    <li>Value chips and AI solution chips enter with small staggered motion.</li>
    <li>AI board includes a scanning line to suggest automation and analysis.</li>
    <li>Process track includes a moving progress rule above the steps.</li>
    <li>Cards and images have hover movement for interactivity.</li>
    <li>The CSS includes prefers-reduced-motion support for accessibility.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>File Map</h2>
  <table>
    <tr>
      <th>Path</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>package.json</td>
      <td>Defines scripts and dependencies for the React/Vite app.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>vite.config.js</td>
      <td>Configures Vite with the React plugin.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>index.html</td>
      <td>HTML shell used by Vite.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>src/main.jsx</td>
      <td>React entry point. Mounts the App component into the root element.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>src/App.jsx</td>
      <td>Main React component. Contains all page sections and text content.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>src/App.css</td>
      <td>Main page styling for the Omekum website.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>src/index.css</td>
      <td>Global CSS imported by the React entry point.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>public/</td>
      <td>Static public assets.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>dist/</td>
      <td>Production build output generated by Vite.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Dependencies</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>react</li>
    <li>react-dom</li>
    <li>vite</li>
    <li>@vitejs/plugin-react</li>
    <li>eslint and React ESLint plugins</li>
  </ul>

